  "details": "Action Menu (PC VR) · Introduced in 2026.3.2, build 1901 (live Sept 1 2026)\n\nSUMMARY\n\nPlease add a setting to turn off the long-press actions that 2026.3.2 added to the Action Menu's buttons, for players who use Flick Select.\n\nPROBLEM\n\nWith Flick Select on (the default), a slice is selected when the thumbstick reaches full deflection. Any flick that isn't very quick now also counts as a long-press, so a normal selection often opens the button's settings sub-menu (e.g. \"Hold to open Personal Mirror settings.\") instead. Turning Flick Select off avoids this, but then every selection needs a trigger press. There's currently no way to get the pre-2026.3.2 behavior back.\n\nPROPOSED SOLUTION\n\nAdd a \"Long-Press Actions\" toggle under Options > Action Menu, next to Flick Select. When it's off, buttons in the radial menu will only toggle similar to pre-2026.3.2 behavior. Reset Avatar still needs its hold, since that one is a safety check.",
